    <sectiondef kind="user-defined">
      <header>TI EHRPWM custom flags</header>
      <description><para>These flags can be used with <computeroutput><ref refid="group__pwm__interface_1gadd9049c9a56cd9419736b3514e42dc01" kindref="member">pwm_set()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__pwm__interface_1gaff280789f7b45fdefc354b3f841fe3ef" kindref="member">pwm_set_cycles()</ref></computeroutput>, or in the devicetree <computeroutput>pwms</computeroutput> property&apos;s flags cell to select how the TI EHRPWM action qualifier pairs its up/down actions.</para>
<para>The custom flags are on the upper 24 bits of the <ref refid="group__pwm__interface_1gae1dcfb878163da76041efcedf0960fa0" kindref="member">pwm_flags_t</ref>, above the bit reserved for <computeroutput><ref refid="group__pwm__interface_1ga2c706bbada711f383d7b42f09dace861" kindref="member">PWM_POLARITY_NORMAL</ref></computeroutput>/<computeroutput><ref refid="group__pwm__interface_1ga930c0ab50f81aeb571af9747947d7fae" kindref="member">PWM_POLARITY_INVERTED</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
</description>
      <memberdef kind="define" id="ti__am3352__ehrpwm_8h_1a2c91175b299365c717f438cd024c2787" prot="public" static="no">
        <name>TI_EHRPWM_USE_AQ_SET_ZRO_PRD</name>
        <initializer><ref refid="group__sys-util_1ga3a8ea58898cb58fc96013383d39f482c" kindref="member">BIT</ref>(8)</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Drive the action qualifier up/down actions from the ZRO/PRD time-base events. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>By default, the action qualifier pairs the up/down actions with the channel&apos;s own compare match (CAU/CAD for channel A, CBU/CBD for channel B). Set this flag to instead pair the up action with the time-base counter equal to zero (ZRO) event and the down action with the time-base counter equal to period (PRD) event. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
